From: jaewun <jaewun@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: rsinput: quiesce the gamepad MCU on suspend

The RSInput gamepad MCU streams reports continuously over its UART. The driver
had a resume handler (re-init the MCU) but no suspend handler, so the MCU kept
transmitting across the system-suspend teardown. While the geni-serial port is
being stopped the RX interrupt storms, the primary handler returns IRQ_NONE,
and the kernel's spurious-interrupt detector ("irqNNN: nobody cared") then
permanently disables the UART IRQ -- leaving the gamepad dead after that resume
until the IRQ is re-requested (driver rebind / reboot).

Add an rsinput_suspend() that drops the MCU enable rail and holds it in reset
(mirroring rsinput_remove) so the line goes silent before the UART suspends;
rsinput_resume() already re-powers and re-initialises it.

Signed-off-by: jaewun <jaewun@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c b/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
index 4772c23af6..e4b6062516 100644
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
@@ -612,6 +612,29 @@ static void rsinput_remove(struct serdev_device *serdev) {
     regulator_disable(drv->vdd);
 }
 
+static int rsinput_suspend(struct device *dev)
+{
+    struct rsinput_driver *drv = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+    /*
+     * The MCU streams gamepad reports continuously over the UART. If it keeps
+     * sending across the system-suspend teardown, the geni-serial RX interrupt
+     * storms while the port is being stopped, the primary handler returns
+     * IRQ_NONE, and the kernel's spurious-IRQ detector permanently disables the
+     * UART IRQ -- leaving the gamepad dead after resume until the IRQ is
+     * re-requested. Quiesce the MCU (drop its enable rail and hold it in reset,
+     * mirroring rsinput_remove) so the line goes silent before the UART
+     * suspends; rsinput_resume() re-powers and re-initialises it.
+     */
+    if (drv->enable_gpio)
+        gpiod_set_value_cansleep(drv->enable_gpio, 0);
+
+    if (drv->reset_gpio)
+        gpiod_set_value_cansleep(drv->reset_gpio, 0);
+
+    return 0;
+}
+
 static int rsinput_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
     struct rsinput_driver *drv = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
@@ -619,7 +642,7 @@ static int rsinput_resume(struct device *dev)
     return rsinput_init_commands(drv);
 }
 
-static DEFINE_SIMPLE_DEV_PM_OPS(rsinput_pm_ops, NULL, rsinput_resume);
+static DEFINE_SIMPLE_DEV_PM_OPS(rsinput_pm_ops, rsinput_suspend, rsinput_resume);
 
 static const struct of_device_id rsinput_of_match[] = {
     { .compatible = "gamepad,rsinput" },
